    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's more than just being sad. it's like... i was never a whole person on my own. we were just one thing. now that he's gone, the \"me\" part is just a void. it feels like i'm just a broken piece of something that doesn't exist anymore. what's even the point of trying to rebuild a person that was never really there to begin with?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're not a broken piece; you are a complete, beautiful piece that was simply intertwined with another. The void you feel is the space where your shared life used to be, and it's a massive space to fill. Instead of trying to rebuild a person who was never whole alone, maybe you can start by finding the quiet, small things that *you* enjoyed before him. Those tiny anchors are the first steps back to being just you.",
      "source": "target",
